use flake

# Bench secrets live outside the repository. `.envrc` is tracked, so anything
# written here is one `git add` away from the history; `.envrc.local` is
# gitignored and holds the SLIX privacy password the `slix` bench command
# needs.
# `TEDDIEBOX_LANGUAGE` picks which of the card's four sets of system sounds the
# box speaks: `de`, `en-gb`, `en-us` or `fr`. It belongs in `.envrc.local`
# rather than here, because it is a property of one box rather than of the
# project, and unset means German. An unrecognised value fails the build.
# `TEDDIEBOX_IDENTITY_DIR` names the directory holding this box's `CLIENT.DER`
# and `PRIVATE.DER` — the certificate and key `just identity` writes into the
# `cert` flash partition. A private key belongs neither here nor on the card,
# so this points somewhere outside the repository and is set in `.envrc.local`.
# Either filename case works; a vfat mount of the card lowercases them.
source_env_if_exists .envrc.local
